    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d979">

                <pb facs="1225" n="1207" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg1207"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.248/1–1946: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Pawley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-01-19T17:00:00-05:00">January 19, 1946—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>64. ReDeptel’s 26, Jan 11, 9 p.m.; 46, Jan
                    17, 8 p.m.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d979-f1"/> General Arnold and General
                        Rowell<anchor n="7" xml:id="d979-f2"/> concur in delivery to Peruvian air
                    force upon their arrival 2 PBY’s or OA–10’s, 5 B–25’s, 10
                    P–47’s, 3 C–47’s, 5 AT–11’s, 2 C–45’s and in addition 5 liaison, and 5 AT–6’s.
                    The balance of the planes allocated to Peru and mentioned in your Deptel 26, Jan 11, 9 p.m. will be held in dead
                    storage Talara Army Air Base, custody of Ambassador, for delivery as and when
                    Air Mission chief and Ambassador agree Air Force can absorb.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pawley</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d979-f1" n="6" xml:id="d979-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d979-f2" n="7" xml:id="d979-f2-content">
                <p>Maj. Gen. Ross E. Rowell, Chief of the United States Military Mission to
                    Peru.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
